{"id":"G2037","lemma":"Ἔραστος","transliteration":"erastos","sayIt":"erastos","language":"Greek","partOfSpeech":"","gloss":"Erastus","meaning":"Ἐραστος, -ου, ὁ\nErastus;\n1. a companion of St. Paul, Act.19:22, and prob. 2Ti.4:20.\n2. The treasurer of Corinth, Rom.16:23.†\n(AS)","glosses":["erastus"],"count":3,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"act-19","v":22,"renderings":{"bsb":"Erastus","kjv":"Erastus"}},{"chapterId":"rom-16","v":23,"renderings":{"bsb":"Erastus","kjv":"Erastus"}},{"chapterId":"2ti-4","v":20,"renderings":{"bsb":"Erastus","kjv":"Erastus"}}],"elsewhere":[{"ref":"Acts 19:22","note":"Having sent into Macedonia two of those who served him, Timothy and Erastus, he himself stayed in Asia for a while.","source":"web"},{"ref":"Romans 16:23","note":"Gaius, my host and host of the whole assembly, greets you. Erastus, the treasurer of the city, greets you, as does Quartus, the brother.","source":"web"},{"ref":"2 Timothy 4:20","note":"Erastus remained at Corinth, but I left Trophimus at Miletus sick.","source":"web"}],"related":[{"id":"G20370","lemma":"ἐνσκηνόω","transliteration":"enskēnoō","gloss":"to encamp"},{"id":"G20371","lemma":"ἐντιμόομαι","transliteration":"entimoomai","gloss":"be held in honour"},{"id":"G20372","lemma":"ἐντιναγμός","transliteration":"entinagmos","gloss":"shaking"},{"id":"G20373","lemma":"ἐντινάσσω","transliteration":"entinassō","gloss":"to collide with"},{"id":"G20374","lemma":"ἐντόσθιος","transliteration":"entosthios","gloss":"inwards, entrails"},{"id":"G20375","lemma":"ἐντότερος","transliteration":"entoteros","gloss":"inner"},{"id":"G20376","lemma":"ἐντυχία","transliteration":"entuchia","gloss":"records"},{"id":"G20377","lemma":"ἐνυποκρίνομαι","transliteration":"enupokrinomai","gloss":"play the hypocrite"}],"sources":["STEPBible TBESH/TBESG lexicon (CC BY 4.0)","STEPBible TAHOT/TAGNT tagged text (CC BY 4.0)"]}